Generic abilities - List in progress

Neighborhood watch and militia should both be location based so they are broadly available but require building up an organization in that specific location.  These should broadly be available to all coop+worker groups (including drones)
Neighborhood watch: bolster police efforts, wont do much if police are corrupt
Militia: bypass police efforts, not vulnerable to police corruption

HQ actions I dont yet know where to put (maybe on advisors?)
When an activist group is played they get two cooldowns.  After a certain period (say 6 months) they automatically get added back into the pool.  After a shorter period (say 3 months) you can chose to put them back into the pool.  This can be triggered anytime, maybe on the advisor card menus.


Coops:
public externalities: for groups with positive externalities like fighting drug addition, scaling them up just directly impacts the relevent values
Scale up: coops can expand operations, helping prosperity in one of two ways
-expand ranks: grow the size of the coop, this is extra effective if the coops in the district have lots of outside employees at the moment
-provide jobs: grow the number of gig employees, particularly focused on the demograpics with the lowest priority.  So this offers a way to address poverty among Otherworlders for instance.


Workers groups:
Mutual Aid - Aide within the group, drones help drones, immigrant associations help other immigrants
Public Aid - This should help within the area and should require the group providing the aid be better off then others in the area

Drone groups:
This is a subset of the workers templates with a couple specific abilities:
Sabotage: ding the relevent big-3 member throughout the city
Strike: Should be a very high bar to do this.  There should be ways to lower the very high bar:
-establish a welfare system
-establish an unemployment system
-channel secret funds to the underground unions
-cut a deal with one or more syndicates to support the strike
Every successful strike would make subsequent strikes less difficult.  After enough of them an independent Labor Board could be established.

Non-drone worker groups:
Sector integration - This should be the advanced unlock where a powerful group with high support can leverage that power for something beneficial citywide.  It's a one time trigger for "powering up" the group.  So if you get good support among the aquaculture workers of the city and they are prospering you can trigger a citywide aquaculture improvement that makes food more affordable throughout the city.



Business groups:
Business groups generally are going to be advanced unlocks however some street level businesses like retail associations might be easy recruits.
But local campaigns: should ding the properity of the big 3 and help prosperity of the city, more effective the better off both the business group is and citywide prosperity is
Investment networks: Helps other businesses throughout the city, impact should be highly reliant on the wealth of the business group.  Even if your convenience store owners are doing great by convenience store standards they dont have that much to invest.  If you get the local elites on board with local investing they might drastically cut capital costs for their poorer counterparts throughout the city
Anti-Racket pledge: this should be limited to the less affluent business groups and like the drones going on strike it should have a hard bar to accomplish.  It should absolutely tank syndicate power in the district.  The weaker the syndicates are the easier this should be to pull off.  The stronger and less corrupt the police/militias, the easier.